    <div class="post-container" id="fpc-2118414">
                      
		<div class="post" id="post-2118414">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,2118414)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-2118414">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="1361261"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1411678572 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 Sep 2014 20:56</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2118414">
									

<p>Like the first entry, this tale lacks any sort of logical underpinning in how any serious organization would operate. I realize that this complaint probably seems bizarre, considering that it's about a tale where wacky mutated animals traipse about after being transformed with designer drug-runoff or whatever the hell is going on.</p>
<p>Thing is, in a situation where wacky occurrences are threatening the established order of things, you need some sort of logical world to serve as the setting; the straight man, if you will. And right now, you have as a protagonist someone that, when faced with scientific impossibilities, has a reaction that's basically &quot;I'm not even supposed to be here today, aw jeeze&quot;. If frustration and annoyance are what greets the impossible occurring, then I wonder why there's a Foundation here. I would probably still downvote a &quot;Serpent's Hand: Animal Control Division&quot; tale, but that would at least make more sense in context with the world you're presenting.</p>
<p>And then there's the &quot;Welcome to the Foundation now, son&quot; thing going on here. Recruitment into highly professional organizations like the Foundation is generally presumed to be, and a paramilitary subsidiary thereof at that, just doesn't work like that. The guy has all of one morning of experience in dealing with this stuff. And then they pile him into the Action Van and literally hand him a gun to go fight monsters. That's about eight bridges too far in terms of my suspension of disbelief, and since I'm not really buying into this as any semblance of a realistic world you're portraying, the crazy monster animals that show up just don't have any real impact to me.</p>
<p>Obviously this in the positive range, and generally speaking the site membership responds better to what you're doing here than I do, but I dunno. I feel like we've got enough crazy, lolwacky off-the-rails shenanigans on the wiki already, and if you're seriously trying to portray the Foundationverse through the eyes of an uninitiated person, then this piece is lacking in that regard.</p>

							</div>

								
					
